IMPORT prelude

-- Energy Conservation Act 2012 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a shop, an importer, a household or a business: the
-- restrictions on supplying and importing regulated goods (ss 12, 12A), how long a registration lasts and how to appeal (ss 15,
-- 17), the maximum fines for the goods offences (ss 12, 12A, 18, 19, 20), registration and cancellation for large energy users
-- (ss 23, 25), the penalty scale for energy-management offences (s 32), an authorised officer's entry to premises (s 33),
-- obstruction (s 38), fuel economy labelling of motor vehicles offered for sale (s 42) and composition (s 74).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to and including 1 December 2021), informal consolidation, version in
-- force from 1 July 2026, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ECA2012.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the deposit is
-- Act 10 of 2026 (wef 1 July 2026), which among other things added the prohibited import for one's own use (s 12(1)(b), (3A)).
-- Act 39 of 2024 (wef 1 December 2025) added registrable relevant persons (s 23A) and s 26B.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0067 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions such a person meets. Not encoded: which goods are regulated and what they must meet
-- (that is all in Gazette orders and regulations under ss 11, 22, 78, none retrieved); the content of the energy management duties
-- in ss 26A to 31 beyond their penalties; s 23A and s 26B registration of relevant persons except their penalty; transport facility
-- operators (Part 4 Division 2) and Part 4 enforcement; s 41 type-approval submissions; information powers (ss 34 to 37, 64 to 66);
-- disclosure (s 71); offences by bodies corporate (s 72); the court's remedial order (s 73); exemptions under ss 61 and 77.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Energy Conservation Act 2012 -- goods, registration and penalties`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `12 -- prohibited supply and prohibited import of regulated goods`

-- s 12(1): "a person must not (a) make a prohibited supply of regulated goods in Singapore ... or (b) make a prohibited import of
-- regulated goods". (2): fine not exceeding $10,000.
-- (3): a prohibited supply is one where "the goods do not comply, on or after the effective date for those goods", with a prescribed
-- requirement in (4) "not waived under section 31B(1)", and the supply is made "(i) in the course or furtherance of the
-- firstmentioned person's trade or business; or (ii) in furtherance of the second-mentioned person's trade or business".
-- (3A) (Act 10 of 2026): a prohibited import is the import of non-complying regulated goods "by the person for the person's own use".
-- (4): the requirements are registration, a minimum energy efficiency standard, labelling, accompanying information, dissemination.
-- (5): (1)(a) does not apply to goods supplied "as part of any premises by the developer", if the developer did not import or
-- manufacture them and they complied "at the time the agreement for the supply of the goods to the developer was entered into"; nor to
-- a supply by a participant in that developer's supply chain if the goods complied when its agreement was made.
-- (6): nor to prescribed goods supplied to a person (not a developer) constructing premises the person will occupy, for use in them,
-- who did not import or manufacture them, if they complied when the agreement was made.
DECLARE Dealing HAS
    `the goods are regulated goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on or after the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prescribed requirement is unmet and not waived` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied in the course of the supplier's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied in furtherance of the recipient's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imported for the importer's own use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied by a developer as part of premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied by a participant in a developer's supply chain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied for premises the recipient is building to occupy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods are prescribed for subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the developer or recipient imported or manufactured the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods complied when the supply agreement was made` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are caught on the date` IF
        `the dealing`'s `the goods are regulated goods`
    AND `the dealing`'s `on or after the effective date`
    AND `the dealing`'s `a prescribed requirement is unmet and not waived`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is a prohibited supply` IF
        `the goods are caught on the date` `the dealing`
    AND (    `the dealing`'s `supplied in the course of the supplier's trade or business`
         OR  `the dealing`'s `supplied in furtherance of the recipient's trade or business`)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a subsection (5) or (6) exception applies` IF
        (    `the dealing`'s `supplied by a developer as part of premises`
         AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `the developer or recipient imported or manufactured the goods`)
         AND `the dealing`'s `the goods complied when the supply agreement was made`)
    OR  (    `the dealing`'s `supplied by a participant in a developer's supply chain`
         AND `the dealing`'s `the goods complied when the supply agreement was made`)
    OR  (    `the dealing`'s `the goods are prescribed for subsection (6)`
         AND `the dealing`'s `supplied for premises the recipient is building to occupy`
         AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `the developer or recipient imported or manufactured the goods`)
         AND `the dealing`'s `the goods complied when the supply agreement was made`)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is a prohibited import` IF
        `the goods are caught on the date` `the dealing`
    AND `the dealing`'s `imported for the importer's own use`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is an offence under section 12` IF
        (    `the dealing is a prohibited supply` `the dealing`
         AND (NOT `a subsection (5) or (6) exception applies` `the dealing`))
    OR  `the dealing is a prohibited import` `the dealing`

§§ `12A -- supply by an unregistered importer or manufacturer`

-- s 12A(1): an importer or manufacturer of regulated goods "must not, in the course of any trade or business, supply those regulated
-- goods in Singapore on or after the effective date for those goods, unless the importer or manufacturer is a registered supplier".
-- (2): fine not exceeding $10,000. This is separate from s 12: compliant goods are still caught if the supplier is unregistered.
GIVEN `is the importer or manufacturer` IS A BOOLEAN, `supplies in the course of trade` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `after the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a registered supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply is an offence under section 12A` IF
        `is the importer or manufacturer` AND `supplies in the course of trade` AND `after the effective date`
    AND (NOT `is a registered supplier`)

§§ `15 and 17 -- duration of registration, and appeals`

-- s 15(1): a supplier's registration "remains valid unless withdrawn or revoked"; (2): the registration of goods, including any
-- renewal, "is valid for 3 years unless earlier withdrawn or revoked"; (3): renewal must be applied for "before the expiry".
GIVEN `is a registration of goods` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since registration or renewal` IS A NUMBER, `withdrawn or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration is still valid` IF
        (NOT `withdrawn or revoked`)
    AND (    (NOT `is a registration of goods`)
         OR  `years since registration or renewal` LESS THAN 3)

-- s 17(1): an aggrieved importer or manufacturer "may, within 14 days after the date of receipt of the notice ... appeal in writing to
-- the Minister". (3): the Minister's decision "is final". (4): a condition or revocation "takes effect from the date specified by the
-- Director-General ... unless the Minister otherwise directs", even though an appeal is pending.
GIVEN `days since receiving the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days since receiving the notice` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revocation takes effect on the date the Director-General specified` IF
    NOT `the Minister directed otherwise`

§§ `12, 12A, 18, 19, 20 -- maximum penalties for the goods offences`

-- s 12(2), 12A(2): $10,000. s 18(3) records: $2,000. s 19(2) failing to provide samples or information: $5,000. s 20 false
-- statements in a registration application, false records, false information: $5,000 "or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 3 months or ... both".
DECLARE GoodsOffence IS ONE OF
    `a prohibited supply or import`
    `supply by an unregistered importer or manufacturer`
    `failing to keep or produce records`
    `failing to provide samples or information`
    `a false statement or false record`

GIVEN `the goods offence` IS A GoodsOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the goods offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the goods offence`
    WHEN `a prohibited supply or import` THEN 10000
    WHEN `supply by an unregistered importer or manufacturer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing to keep or produce records` THEN 2000
    WHEN `failing to provide samples or information` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a false statement or false record` THEN 5000

GIVEN `the goods offence` IS A GoodsOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for the goods offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the goods offence`
    WHEN `a false statement or false record` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `23 and 25 -- registering, and leaving the register`

-- s 23(1): a corporation which qualifies as a registrable corporation "must, within the period specified in the order under section
-- 22(1), apply"; (4) failing to do so: fine not exceeding $5,000. s 23A(4): the same $5,000 for a registrable relevant person.
-- s 25(1): a registered corporation may apply to cancel "(a) subject to paragraph (b), if [it] no longer qualifies"; "(b) in the case
-- where the registered corporation had qualified ... by reason of any business activity or premises ... having attained an energy use
-- threshold, if that business activity or premises ... ceased to attain the energy use threshold for a continuous period of at least
-- 3 years immediately preceding the application". (2): the Director-General "must cancel" if a ground is made out.
GIVEN `qualified by reaching an energy use threshold` IS A BOOLEAN, `no longer qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `continuous years below the threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation may apply to cancel its registration` IF
    IF `qualified by reaching an energy use threshold`
    THEN `continuous years below the threshold` AT LEAST 3
    ELSE `no longer qualifies`

§§ `32 -- penalties for energy-management offences`

-- s 32(1): for offences under s 26A(3) (as to s 26A(1)(b), submitting the new-venture report), 26B(4) (as to 26B(2)(b) or (3)(b),
-- submitting reports), 27(2), 27A(2), 27B(2), 28(3), 29(3), 30(5) or 31A(3): "(a) on the first conviction ... a fine not exceeding
-- $10,000; and (b) on a second or subsequent conviction ... a fine not exceeding $20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after that second or
-- subsequent conviction".
-- (3): s 26A(3) as to s 26A(1)(a), not conducting the new-venture energy efficiency opportunities assessment: "$100,000".
-- (4): s 26B(4) as to 26B(2)(a) or (3)(a), not assessing or monitoring a prescribed system, or not doing the directed maintenance:
-- "$20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... $500 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction".
-- (5): s 31, false data: "$5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or ... both".
-- The "related provision" rules of (2) for convictions under the pre-2018 text are not modelled.
DECLARE ManagementOffence IS ONE OF
    `no new-venture energy efficiency assessment`
    `no new-venture assessment report`
    `no assessment or monitoring of a prescribed system`
    `no maintenance as directed for a prescribed system`
    `no report on a prescribed system`
    `no periodic energy use report`
    `no energy management system`
    `no energy efficiency opportunities assessment`
    `no energy efficiency improvement plan`
    `no records kept`
    `no energy manager appointed`
    `no resubmission as directed`
    `falsified data`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A ManagementOffence, `previously convicted` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 32` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `no new-venture energy efficiency assessment` THEN 100000
    WHEN `no assessment or monitoring of a prescribed system` THEN 20000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    WHEN `no maintenance as directed for a prescribed system` THEN 20000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    WHEN `falsified data` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE
        IF `previously convicted`
        THEN 20000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
        ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A ManagementOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment under section 32` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `falsified data` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `33 -- entering premises`

-- s 33(a): an authorised officer, on declaring the office and producing the identification card, may "enter any premises (i) during
-- normal business hours without notice; or (ii) at any other time after giving not less than 6 hours' previous notice to the occupier
-- ... (unless the occupier has consented to a shorter period of notice)".
GIVEN `during normal business hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of notice given` IS A NUMBER, `occupier consented to shorter notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `identification card produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may enter` IF
        `identification card produced`
    AND (    `during normal business hours`
         OR  `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 6
         OR  `occupier consented to shorter notice`)

§§ `38 -- obstruction`

-- s 38: hindering or obstructing the Director-General or an authorised officer: "(a) ... a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or ... both; and (b) in the case of a second or subsequent conviction, ... a fine
-- not exceeding $20,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or ... both". The prison term does not rise.
GIVEN `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstruction` MEANS
    IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

§§ `42 -- fuel economy labels on motor vehicles for sale`

-- s 42(1): a person "must not, in the course of any trade or business, sell or offer for sale" a motor vehicle of a class in an order
-- under s 40 on or after the FEL effective date, unless "(a) throughout the period that the motor vehicle is displayed for sale, the
-- motor vehicle bears the label ... approved by the Registrar"; and "(b) any printed promotional material or advertisement" contains
-- the prescribed fuel economy and emissions information. (2): fine not exceeding $2,000.
GIVEN `sold in the course of trade` IS A BOOLEAN, `of a class in a section 40 order and after the FEL date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `labelled throughout the display` IS A BOOLEAN, `printed advertising carries the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale is an offence under section 42` IF
        `sold in the course of trade` AND `of a class in a section 40 order and after the FEL date`
    AND (    (NOT `labelled throughout the display`)
         OR  (NOT `printed advertising carries the information`))

§§ `74 -- composition`

-- s 74(1): an offence under the Act "(except Part 4)" that is prescribed as compoundable may be compounded "by collecting ... a sum
-- not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b)
-- $5,000". (Part 4 offences have their own s 60, not read.)
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
